OL,3,ANHS trust apologises for Noah Woods
OL,4,Adata breach
OL,5,
OL,6,FAn NHS trust has apologised to the
OL,7,Ffamily of three-year-old Noah Woods for
OL,8,Fthe "extra anguish" caused after a data
OL,9,Fbreach of his medical records.
OL,11,FLaunching an "urgent" investigation, Dr
OL,12,FMartin Mansfield, deputy chief medical
OL,13,Fofficer at East Suffolk and North Essex
OL,14,FNHS Foundation Trust, said that any
OL,15,Funauthorised access of patient data was
OL,16,F"completely unacceptable".
OL,18,FDisciplinary action will be taken if
OL,19,Fneeded, the statement from the trust
OL,20,Fadded.
OL,23,APub: 27-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG6/40
